# @auki/$crate_package_name

wasm-bindgen JavaScript bindings for `auki-logs`.

```js
import init, { canonicalManifestJson, encodeSegmentEntriesJson } from "./$generated_js_file";

await init();

const manifest = canonicalManifestJson(JSON.stringify({
  kind: "example",
  segment_duration_ns: 1000000000,
  retention_ns: 3000000000,
}));
const segment = encodeSegmentEntriesJson(
  0,
  JSON.stringify([{ timestamp_ns: 100, payload_hex: "7061796c6f6164" }]),
);
```

The package exposes pure manifest and segment-byte helpers. Filesystem log
read/write/tail helpers are native-only through UniFFI; browser persistence
needs a storage adapter before it belongs in the wasm surface.
